n. We're all used to working in air-conditioned rooms, so carrying luggage for fifteen minutes in this heat is quite a heavy workout for us.\" [432] \"Ms. Nogi can ride alone.\" A graduate student said, \"We'll walk slowly.\" [433] \"After going up the slope, take the first left turn at the intersection, and then it's just one straight path. Keep going and you'll reach the campsite. There are signs along the way, so you won't get lost.\" Yae opened the car door and said. [434] \"I want to walk too.\" Nogi Yuzuki, who was twirling her parasol, said. [435] \"Please go take a seat in the car.\" Sugawara said, and Nogi Yuzuki reluctantly got into the car. [436] The road was not paved, and the van reached the campsite in three minutes. There was a two-story reinforced concrete building on the slope that looked like it was about to collapse. A small sign read \"Campsite\" and pointed to a narrow path. The car couldn't go any further. [437] \"This building used to be the center for wild camping activities. It has a dining hall, toilets, and showers, but now it's empty. There are tents and other equipment in the warehouse over there. We brought the gas cylinders this morning and checked them. The showers are fine too. There's electricity here as well. Sometimes we come here to camp, especially when we want to get out of the research institute. This is the only way to get around the island.\" [438] \"Thank you for the trouble,\" said Mr. Awakura as he got off the van from the back. The umbrella girl and Mr. Shiozaki unloaded the luggage, and Mr. Nakajima helped them. [439] \"There's no phone here, so if you need anything, come find me at the research institute. I have some work to do and will be back later. I'll come back in the evening to bother you again...\"\n[440] The four-wheel drive van drove away down the slightly sloping road and disappeared. Suddenly, the surroundings fell silent. Although you couldn't see the sea, you could hear the sound of the waves. [441] There 