d a knife since her elementary school labor class, so the male students did it for her. When the tent was set up and the oil sizzled on the iron plate, all the students gathered around the fire except for Miharu. [452] \"Oh, where is Xizhi Yuan?\" Sugawara spread the bean sprouts on the iron plate and looked around, \"It seems that only she is not here...\"\n[453] \"She said she went for a walk over there...\" one male student answered, \"Because she couldn't help.\" [454] The students opened the refrigerator brought by Miharu and took out the beer inside. Because there was dry ice in the refrigerator, the beer was too cold. The smoke made the students on the downwind side rub their eyes. It was already quite dark at six o'clock, probably because the trees were too dense. [455] \"Are you okay...\" Sugawara handed the chopsticks to the student and left the fire. [456] \"Sh\u00ec x\u012b zh\u012b yu\u00e1n ma?\" H\u00ed zh\u014dng y\u012b sh\u01d2u ch\u00ed zhe p\u00ed ji\u01d4 y\u00ec l\u0101 gu\u00e0n w\u00e0ng w\u00e1ng yu\u01cen f\u0101ng, \"y\u01d0 d\u0101o hu\u00ed l\u00e1i le.\" [457] \"D\u014du shu\u014d t\u0101 b\u0101ng b\u00f9 sh\u00e0ng b\u0101ng y\u011b, k\u00f9 q\u00ec le ba\u2026\u2026\" X\u012b chu\u0101n shu\u014d. [458] X\u012b chu\u0101n zh\u01d0 h\u0113 le b\u00e0n g\u01d4 p\u00ed ji\u01d4 li\u01cen ji\u00f9 t\u014dng h\u00f3ng le. Zh\u00e8 sh\u00ed x\u012b zh\u012b yu\u00e1n xi\u00e0o zhe hu\u00ed l\u00e1i le. [459] \"X\u012b zh\u012b yu\u00e1n ji\u011b jie, y\u00e0o li\u01ceo le a, n\u01d0 k\u00e0n.\" Yu\u00e1n ti\u00e1n s\u00f2ng y\u012b g\u01d4 p\u00ed ji\u01d4 q\u00ed y\u01d4 t\u0101, \"ku\u00e0i zi h\u00e9 p\u00e1n zi z\u00e0i n\u00e0 bi\u0101n.\" [460] X\u012b zh\u012b yu\u00e1n ji\u0113 gu\u00f2 p\u00ed ji\u01d4 xi\u00e0o le xi\u00e0o, m\u00e9i sh\u00e9n me shu\u014d le. [461] \"What's wrong with you?\" Shu looked at Mingei and asked. [462] Mingei pointed to her lips and said in a muffled voice, \"I'm eating chocolate.\" [463] \"Ah?\" Shuangduan drank beer and shouted, \"Miss, do you eat chocolate without chewing?\" [464] Mingei narrowed her eyes and nodded, \"It will get worms in my teeth. I absolutely don't chew chocolate... 'Chewing chocolate' is not in my dictionary.\" [465] \"No one's dictionary has it.\" Shu walked towards Mingei. \"You went to the research institute, didn't you?\" [466] Sitting on a log, Momiji said, \"Yeah, last time I came by helicopter and landed on the roof, I didn't see any windows. I walked around once, but there was no one. It's like a power station...\"\n[467] Shuzui sat down next to Momiji and lit the cigarette in his mouth. A student was busy taking pictures of everyone. [468] \"The magazine had featured that building before, like a pile of cement. There's a ramp at the entrance,\" Shuzui said. [469] \"Right,\" Momiji replied. It seemed like she had finished eating the chocolate. She opened a can of beer and drank it. \"Ah, it's delicious. The tent is also nice. I can enjoy it comfortably...\"\n[470] \"You still say that!\" Taneda said while avoiding the smoke, \"Why don't you just go get it yourself?\" [471]\"Teacher, I... thought about the doll thing...\" \"Do you know a novel called 'Phantasm'? (Note: This is a translation of the Japanese title 'Dream Wild Long lasting Work' which translates to 'Dream Wild Long lasting Work' in English.)\" [472]\u3000\u3000\"I don't know, I've just heard the name. It's a mystery novel, right?\" Xianchuan took a sip of beer. He realized that his mind was a bit fuzzy. He had no resistance to alcohol at all. [473]\u3000\u3000\"That's right, it's the best mystery novel by a guy named Mengyao Chuozu. It's an old work\u2026\" Menghui explained, \"It talks about people being bewitched by foxes. When someone is guarding a corpse at night, the corpse goes out into the yard and causes trouble\u2026 Actually, it's the guard who unconsciously plays with the corpse, like playing with a doll. That is, they think the corpse is moving, but it's actually their own hands moving.\" [474]\u3000\u3000\"Wait, I don't quite understand what you're saying.\" Xianchuan said, his face flushed. \"Why would a living person play with a dead body? What's the point?\" [475]\u3000\u3000\"This, maybe because of excessive fatigue\u2026 like sleepwalking.\" Menghui tilted her head. \"I can't remember too clearly, and it's a bit hard to believe\u2026 Anyway, it's about playing with the corpse and only remembering that the corpse is moving, like playing with a doll\u2026 Yeah, do you understand what I mean?\" [476] \"Because Dr. Akira said the killer was a doll, I remembered.\" Momo said, taking a sip from the can, \"Dr. Akira said she saw a doll kill her parents. In reality, she was that doll, and her consciousness left her body and saw... \"\n[477] \"Interesting... but the facts can't be changed.\" Nishikawa took another sip of beer, he could only drink one can at most, \"Regardless of the consciousness, Dr. Akira's act of killing cannot be changed. There were witnesses, and the trial has ended. It's been fifteen years ago. I'm not interested in that. I'm more interested in what happened to her afterwards. Isolated from society for fifteen years. I really want to see her... \"\n[478] \"Here you go, Nishikawa.\" The graduate student, Hida, walked over with a plate of meat and vegetables and chopsticks. [479] \"Ah, thank you, Hida.\" Momo put the beer on the ground and took the plate with both hands. [480] \"Hida, don't spoil her!\" Tateuchi smiled from afar. [481] Aoi held the chopsticks in her left hand and took a bite, exclaiming, \"Delicious! Who made the seasoning?\" [482] \"No seasoning. It's just barbecue sauce,\" Hinata answered. [483] \"Who made the sauce?\" Aoi asked again, \"It's not just soy sauce, right?\" [484] \"Barbecue sauce isn't made by anyone, it's bought,\" Tanaka said, placing the stir-fried noodles on the hot plate. The exchange student, Xiao Wu, was cutting cabbage on the other side of the hot plate. [485] \"Oh? There's barbecue sauce for sale?\u2026\" Aoi stood up and walked over to the hot plate, \"Wow! Stir-fried noodles! I've never had them before\u2026\"\n[486] \"What, you've never eaten stir-fried noodles?\" Kawajiri exclaimed. Everyone sighed again. [487] 5\n[488] The moonlight was bright, and Shimizu was smoking contentedly. He had prepared a large pack of cigarettes for the three-day trip. He smoked a lot. [489] The students divided into three groups, slowly sipping the whisky they brought and chatting. It was cool, like slightly air-conditioned, and fortunately, there were no mosquitoes. No one went into the tent, and everyone was comfortably enjoying themselves outside. [490] Except for the dark sky around them. Shimizu put down the drink and began to sip the slightly cooler cola. The vice director of the research institute, Yamauchi, hadn't arrived yet. Everyone was eagerly waiting for the ice cream that Momo drew from the fridge with dry ice, while waiting for Yamauchi's arrival. [491] At around 8:00 p.m., a helicopter's propeller sound could be heard in the sky. It sounded close but couldn't be seen. The sound gradually faded away to the north. [492] \"It's the research institute's helicopter,\" Yamanaka said, looking up at the sky. \"That's the sound of a jet helicopter.\" [493] Yamanaka was familiar with various engine sounds. She often said that she liked the sound of car and motorcycle engines. Because she liked the sound of engines, her car didn't have a sound system or a radio. [494] As the night deepened, the topic naturally, or rather consciously, turned to strange stories. [495] With graduate student Tamura at the center, everyone took turns telling short stories. However, since they were all science students, they were not good at this, and the atmosphere was not lively. The most frightened was graduate student Hirose, but the three female students were not so bad. The foreign student, Xiaowu, didn't understand much Japanese, and the assistant professor, Kari, couldn't react much either, so the boys put their hopes in Yamanaka. However, they failed. There was no one who had seen a ghost or UFO, and no one believed in it. Yamanaka said that she was more afraid of difficult Chinese characters than ghosts, and everyone laughed. She said, \"The two Chinese characters I'm most afraid of are 'pinyin'.\" [496] However, there were still some people who continued to tell made-up stories until Professor Kuni said, \"Stupid, what's the point?\" [497] It was almost ten o'clock, and it seemed that Yamanaka would not come. So everyone started eating ice cream. After finishing, Akane, Xiao Wu, and Professor Kuni went to the small building of the campsite to take a bath. When they came back, most of the students had gone to the tents. [498] Kurokawa was still not sleepy. He wanted to smoke the last cigarette before going into the tent. [499] Professor Kuni and Xiao Wu went to the female students' tent. Akane put her things in the tent and then walked towards Kurokawa. Upon closer inspection, everyone else was gone except for them. [500] \"Everyone is quite observant,\" Akane sat on a log next to Kurokawa. [501] \"Just pretend I didn't hear that. Everyone was tired after a day of work,\" Sui River exhaled smoke and looked at the sky, \"So many stars. I haven't seen such a beautiful sky in fifteen years, unbelievable.\" [502] Sui River was a little surprised by his own words, as he had never seen the real Arida Shiki in his mind. [503] \"Not only Dr. Arida, but also the people in the research institute are probably watching the screen,\" Momo also looked at the sky. [504] \"But that way of life may not be bad,\" Sui River said, \"Feeling that nature is beautiful in itself is unnatural, which means life is dirty. Only by living in a place separated from nature, without windows, can one discover one's own beauty. Because of doing boring work and living a dirty life, one wants to be praised for something natural.\" [505] \"Such a scene may become virtual at any time, and people will have to appreciate it in the house,\" Momo said, \"But generally, people will have a sense of resistance...\"\n[506] \"Most people will think that nature is fake,\" Shuai Cui lit another cigarette. \"But nature is all fake. People must accept the natural made by computers. Although it's deceiving... but humans should realize that there is no real... going around criticizing the loss of humanity is nonsense. Computers are the most human-like and the most natural among the tools humans have created.\" [507] \"Teacher, can I smoke a cigarette?\" Miao Hua smiled. \"Is your 'deceiving' referring to something that's good for people?\" [508] \"I don't like the word, but yes, I guess so,\" Shuai Cui said. \"Don't smoke, you're not old enough.\" [509] Miao Hua pouted her lips. \"I'll be twenty soon.\" [510] \"When the pliers were first invented, some stubborn people said that using pliers was inhumane. They said that using such a tool was a sign of decline. Even fire, at first, some ethnic groups firmly refused. But we are a species that uses tools, and we can't go back. It is those who criticize loneliness and emptiness that have lost their humanity.\" [511] \"But isn't nuclear energy a problem?\" asked Momiji, hugging her knees. [512] \"It is a problem that the energy is too great,\" said Sugiyama. \"But fire is also dangerous and pollutes the environment. Hydroelectric power, wind power, and solar cells all destroy the environment. Humans cannot live cleanly. We are creatures that destroy the environment, and we were chosen by nature because of our ability to destroy it. It's just a matter of speed. To slow down the destruction of the environment, we must conserve energy. And... we should use computers in all aspects to ensure energy. To protect humanity, we can only rely on virtual reality technology. We must first deceive ourselves, then we can talk about pursuing humanity. Everyone should stay at home and not move objects...\"\n[513] \"Dr. Akagi also said the same thing.\" [514] \"Because it's self-evident,\" said Sugiyama. \"I just used simple words to explain it to you... that understanding is correct. As researchers, we don't produce anything and don't bear any responsibility, but we are the ones who can think about what will happen in a hundred or two hundred years.\" [515] \"There is laughter coming from the tent. They seem to be playing cards by the light of a flashlight.\" [516] \"Do you also think that the research institute is an ideal working place?\" [517] \"Yes, I do,\" Akasaka replied. \"I don't like meeting people if possible.\" [518] \"But please don't go to such a place,\" said Momo. \"You always do what you want to do\u2026\"\n[519] \"You too,\" said Akasaka, smiling. \"Don't worry too much. I can't do that. I have a more mundane side, you know. For example, I smoke and drink coffee. My lifestyle is not very reasonable.\" [520] \"But you don't watch TV or read newspapers,\" said Momo, worried. \"It seems you only think about research.\" [521] \"That's not true. I'm talking to you right now, aren't I?\" Kenji stood up.\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 6:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:47:35 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \nAs long as there's an internet connection, she could be anywhere. Even a tea room with a keyboard...\"\n[3798] \"But her face appeared on the screen too...\" Shibuchi said hurriedly. [3799] \"That could be a recording... She probably recorded the data on the workstation beforehand. She completely escaped... There's no point in looking for her in the research center or on the island.\" [3800] \"When you were playing VR car racing, was it done remotely on a computer?\" Hanae asked. [3801] \"Yes\u2026 You can operate from anywhere.\" Nakagawa answered. [3802] \"But she also sent her voice, so it must have been from a workstation somewhere.\" Mitani said, \"It's probably not a university's computer center\u2026 Anyone can go in there, can't they?\" [3803] \"The voice could have been sent over the phone and a simulated computer.\" Mizuhara stroked his chin, \"Using one of the institute's machines as the main host\u2026 Controlling it over the phone and the internet\u2026\"\n[3804] \"Why did Shinobu Futaba run away?\" The head of the department, Nishiyama, asked in a low voice. [3805] \"Because she's the murderer.\" Nakagawa answered, \"She's the one who killed three people. No, all of this was her doing. Detective-san, you should contact your department right away. It's already too late\u2026\"\n[3806] The Shimizu nodded, wide-eyed. [3807] \"Genius... a genius,\" said Sugawara, nodding repeatedly. \"She won't be swayed by our ideas... she's been ahead from the start...\"\n[3808] \"But Future-san only speaks English, doesn't she?\" asked the head of the West Garden. [3809] \"She's a genius...\" Sugawara smiled. Then, he blew smoke rings with the cigarette in his hand. [3810] \"She's Dr. Akira Miyuki.\" [3811] 8\n[3812] Zuo Chi and Shiyuzhuang said \"We'll be right back\" and left the room. After that, no one in the chief's office spoke. [3813] Xucun remembered it was summer. [3814] The university was on summer vacation. Of course, even though it was summer vacation, it only meant there were no classes. Generally, scholars like Xucun, who are research-oriented, don't even realize it's summer vacation, let alone Obon. Xucun's research lab had windows, but it was basically the same as the True Ardor Research Institute. [3815] He smoked, thinking about what he would think about when he returned to the university. The murder case had ended. At least, Xucun's interest in this case had quickly disappeared. [3816] Detective Shimizu picked up the helicopter model on the chief's desk. [3817] \"The helicopter was invented by Leonardo da Vinci,\" Detective Shimizu said to himself, \"before the airplane. It's strange that it took humans so long to realize the principles of flight... At one point, they thought that birds flapping their wings pushed air downward... That was the reason for the failure...\"\n[3818] No one paid attention to Detective Shimizu's words, except for Yoshiko, who chuckled quietly in the corner. Miyuki seemed a little worried and approached Detective Shimizu. [3819] \"Teacher...\" Miyuki said, \"You said that Dr. Shinjiro Ardor was the murderer...\"\n[3820] \"Yes,\" Detective Shimizu put the helicopter model back on the table and exhaled smoke from one hand. \"I'm not an expert in this field, so I don't know the specifics of multiple personalities... No, I mean, what's physically going on. But, originally, there are multiple personalities within one individual, right? Some people might not believe it, but at least for me... I have many different personalities. I personally believe that very few people have a single personality...\"\n[3821] There was still no reaction from everyone to Xiangchuan's words. [3822] Xiangchuan turned around and spoke to everyone. [3823] \"I mentioned that Japan is a liquid society and the West is a solid society, and this can also be applied to individuals... The Japanese, their multiple personalities within their bodies are like liquids mixed together and stirred. The West's thoughts are not like that. They are still solid. Will Japan gradually become solid in the future?\" [3824] Yes, Shigemori had said that solid things become liquid when looked at for a long time. Xiangchuan remembered. [3825] \"Teacher, what are you talking about?\" Doctor Gakushou stroked his beard. [3826] \"Nothing, just daydreaming,\" Sekigawa said, extinguishing his cigarette. \"What are you all doing?\" [3827] The head of the West office, Nishiyama, opened the door and stepped out, followed by a crestfallen Tsuzuki. [3828] \"Can you explain it to us, teacher?\" Tsuzuki approached Sekigawa. [3829] \"Explain what?\" Sekigawa asked. [3830] \"What you said\u2026\" Tsuzuki exaggeratedly said, \"We've taken emergency measures in Aichi and Mie prefectures to capture Aragaki Futaba\u2026 But I don't understand. Can you explain it to us?\" [3831] \"Yes, I don't understand what you mean either.\" Bowayong said. [3832] Shuzhuo lit a cigarette. \"Everything is clear.\" [3833] \"Teacher...,\" Menghui walked over and whispered softly, \"We need not just the answer, but also your explanation...\"\n[3834] \"Ah, so that's it...,\" Shuzhuo nodded, \"Does everyone need it?\" [3835] Everyone in the room nodded. Shuzhuo was surprised. [3836] \"Alright then\u2026\" X\u012bchu\u01cen puffed out smoke rings as he slowly walked towards the center of the room. \"Where should I start? Ah, let's start by explaining why Red Magic went out of control first\u2026\"\n[3837] \"I already understand that,\" said Mizukami. \"Red Magic is a Trojan horse itself\u2026\"\n[3838] \"I have a question about this,\" said M\u00e9ngr\u00ec, raising her hand like a student. No, she was a true student. \"At that time, Dr. Akagi said that everything became 'F' that day, right? The calendar of the lady computer also had this. So, what is 'F'?\" [3839] \"F is fifteen,\" X\u012bchu\u01cen answered immediately. [3840] \"Fifteen? Is it fifteen?\" M\u00e9ngr\u00ec furrowed her eyebrows. \"Is it the 'F' of fifteen? But\u2026if so, there are many 'F's in fourteen (fourteen), five (five), and four (four).\" [3841] \"It's hexadecimal, Oshimura.\" Fujisawa answered. \"In the Red Magic program, the variable used to calculate time is integer, which means it's an integer type. Computers process numbers in binary, but the program groups four digits together and represents them in hexadecimal. That's one bit. In general integer types, it's two bytes\u2026 because there are four bits, so in hexadecimal, we can use four digits, which means we can use all numbers up to 16 raised to the power of four.\" [3842] \"16 raised to the power of four?\" Yuria questioned. \"That's 65536\u2026 Is that the 256 times 256 calculation you mentioned?\" [3843] \"That's right, that's the resolution, the threshold. I can still remember 16 squared\u2026 In the program, the integer-type variable, if it's an unsigned integer, starts from 0 and goes up to positive integers. Double-precision integers can go up to 8 bits, while single-precision short integers can only go up to 4 bits. Starting from 0, that means the largest number is 65535, which is one less than 65536.\" [3844] \"What does that have to do with F?\" Yuria asked. [3845] \"In hexadecimal, the number on the ones place goes up to 15\u2026\" Fujisawa said. \"But we only have the numbers 0 to 9 in the decimal system. In the decimal system, 10 is a two-digit number. 10 is represented by 1 and 0. In hexadecimal, 16 starts to become a two-digit number 10 (one zero). If we only use the numbers 0 to 9, hexadecimal cannot be used. So\u2026 in general, the numbers 10 to 15 are represented by the letters A, B, C, D, E, F. F is the 15 in the decimal system. Just like the 9 in the decimal system, F is the largest single digit in hexadecimal.\" [3846] \"So everything becomes 15...?\" M\u00e8nghu\u00ec seemed to be confused again. [3847] \"In the 1 to 10, 7 is alone...\" Xiyuan remembered Ms. Truehata's words and said, \"From 1 to 16... B and D become alone...\"\n[3848] \"B is 11, D is 13.\" M\u00e8nghu\u00ec answered, \"Ah, that's right... If it's within 16, 7 is no longer alone. Because there's 14... Dr. Truehata was talking about that... But what if everything becomes F?\" [3849] \"The maximum value of a single-precision integer type in the decimal system, 65535, is represented as FFFF in hexadecimal, which is the largest four-digit number. Counting from 0000, we can count up to all the digits becoming F... Counting until all the digits become F is the timer. This is the limit device. Dr. Truehata planned this at least seven years ago. From Dr. Truehata's room, there is no way to tamper with the system. But Dr. Truehata participated in the development of that system. The limit device is set to 65535 hours after the start, which is 65535 hours later. Dr. Truehata's sand timer started before 65535 hours that day.\" [3850] Xiyuan continued to look at everyone. \"The rest is the same as what Xiyuan said on the cloud. The anomaly in Red Magic was not caused by human intervention, but was set up in the program. That day, the yellow door couldn't be opened. Then, at the predetermined time, the door automatically opened. Because it was a performance, the lighting was dimmed and brightened. Everything was set up. However, for Deborah, who was developed after that, everything was an unforeseen error. Please check the source code of Red Magic carefully. The evidence is still there.\" [3851] 9\n[3852] \"Okay, let's move on to Dr. Momota's puzzle in the room...\" Fujisawa unconsciously walks around the room. This is a habit of his when teaching. \"However, Mr. Nishiyama has basically revealed the truth. In Dr. Momota's room, there was someone else besides Dr. Momota. And from the environmental conditions, we conclude that the person is Dr. Momota's child.\" [3853] \"Wait, wait...,\" Shibazaki raises his hand, \"But it was said that it's impossible...\"\n[3854] \"Wait, I don't accept it,\" Fujisawa says as he walks and looks down, \"When I accept a question, I always say this...\"\n[3855] Shibazaki looks at the department head, Nishiyama, with a bitter smile, but the department head's expression remains unchanged. [3856] \"There is a robot named MICHIRU in the inner bedroom...\u201d Nishida continued, \"It can unlock and lock. This has been confirmed. But why create this robot?\u201d\n[3857] \"It was a playmate for the child...\u201d Momiji immediately said. [3858] \"I acknowledge your statement...\u201d Nishida smiled, \"But that's secondary. I believe the initial motive was not this. It is likely that someone locked the bedroom door from the inside. Then they fell asleep. Therefore, Dr. 