ry?\" [4023] \"Your spirit would not allow such a contradiction, wouldn't it?\" Shichiri deeply blinked her eyes, appearing quite charming, \"However, my child cried when he was born.\" [4024] \"You did those things to die, right?\" Shichiri asked nervously. [4025] \"Yes, it was the starting point of freedom...\"\n[4026] \"You'll turn yourself in to the police, right?\" [4027] \"If I turn myself in, it may not be a death sentence\u2026\" Shiki put her hands on her face, \"Can you tell me when the execution will be? I want to write my own death date on the calendar\u2026 Do you still have such a luxurious schedule?\" [4028] \"Why, you yourself\u2026 That\u2026 why don't you commit suicide?\" [4029] \"Maybe, I want someone else to kill me\u2026\" Shiki gazed off into the distance, \"I want someone else to interfere with my life. That's what love means, isn't it? Shiki-sensei\u2026 No one is born according to their own will. Dying because of someone else's interference is a kind of instinctive desire not to be born according to one's own will, isn't it?\" [4030] \"I understand the reason\u2026\"\n[4031] \"When my parents died, they probably thought the same thing. It was just too sudden, I was a bit surprised\u2026\"\n[4032] \"But I still can't understand.\" Professor Saitou threw his cigarette butt into the ashtray, \"But, why can't I understand? Because my brain is programmed that way. Maybe you're right.\" [4033] \"I'm right, you're wrong\u2026\" Satsuki said, \"Anyway, the concept of being right is just a matter of degree.\" [4034] \"Professor Saitou, why did you come to see me?\" [4035] \"Because what you said in the sea was to my liking\u2026You said that you can't smoke in the water. That wasn't in my predictions. The reason is just that\u2026Professor Saitou, you\u2026you think slowly, but you have excellent directionality. Although your judgment is weak, you have exceptional objectivity. Maybe there are several of you? There are all kinds of Professor Saitous\